{
  "abstract": "For every integer r ≥ 3, the closure in the real line of the ordinary Turán densities of individual finite r-uniform hypergraphs contains a closed interval of positive length. Each forbidden hypergraph has at least one edge. Its density is the limit of the maximum edge count of an n-vertex hypergraph avoiding an injective copy, divided by n choose r. This formalizes Theorem 1.1 of Chen and Liu.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Xizhi Liu"
    }
  ],
